  "_comment": "INTAKE (accordion, 3x2x1): a two-cell-high cargo intake face three cells long, a simple opening with no shelf. Hollow body open on -Z (the section face convention), steel frame ring on the face, gunmetal shell that ENDS behind the ring so no face shares its plane (the example's z-fight fix), a lit strip under the lintel, amber hazard blocks on the sill. Two leaves of six slats across the long face, named nodes intake_slat_l0..l5 and intake_slat_r0..r5, REST SHUT so the cell-box check grades the closed door. Each slat node is placed rotate [0,0,90], so its local X runs up the slat: a fold is a local RotateX plus a slide toward its pocket, the IntakeDoor track's Fold motion. Fully open, the pleat tips of neighbouring slats in one leaf overlap by up to one slat thickness; that is accepted, slat-frame and non-neighbour overlap are not. Promoted: the cargo_intake_section render mesh.",
